  "Data display 1": "NOT STARTED (budget). 18 sets remain: Kbd, Kbd group, Badge, Badge / kind, Avatar, Avatar presence, Avatar group, Item, Item group, .Item icon tile, .Item image, Card, Stat card, Table header cell, Table cell, Table row, Table, Data table. Then the DD1 sweep: Kbd into Menu item shortcut, Tooltip kbd, Command item/palette, Search kbd; Badge plain into Tab/Nav item counts, Badge subtle into Combobox chips; Avatar into Hover card, Sidebar footer, Top bar."
 },
 "deviations": [
  "Actions: instance-swap defaults (iconStartGlyph, iconEndGlyph, glyph, Icon glyph, Action bar actions) point at the Fluent equivalents (Fluent/Icon/<same base name>, Fluent/.Action bar / actions), not the base glyphs; property names unchanged.",
  "Actions: a glyph chosen by override on a base instance survives the swap as the base (Lucide) glyph; re-pick the Fluent/Icon/* glyph after swapping. FSI vectors are named 'fsi' so Fluent glyph tints never land on a swapped-in Lucide glyph.",
  "Actions: all FSI glyphs use the 16 Regular drawing scaled to 12/20 (arrow_enter_left and circle_small use the 20 drawing; spinner_ios 16). Filled twins exist as Fluent/Icon/<name>-filled but are not variant-bound: the glyph is an instance-swap property shared by all variants, so Toggle/Icon toggle selected cannot switch to the Filled twin by itself.",
  "Actions: coordinator decision applied: Toggle and Icon toggle selected=true use the accent face (F.accent) in both default and outline variants; brief's F.neutral latched recipe superseded.",
  "Actions: Button group items are AppBarButtons (Fluent ghost) instead of the base outline face, so the gap-0 CommandBar row reads as WinUI and never as a joined group. separator is now a 25\u00d7H frame holding a 1\u00d720 'rule' (12 each side); same layer name and boolean binding.",
  "Actions: Toggle gained theme-only boolean property 'pill' and part 'pill' (16\u00d73 accent), used only by Fluent/Toggle group segmented (SelectorBar).",
